title: Keyboard shortcuts
description: Every shortcut for viewing, finding and annotating — and how to remap them.
---

<script lang="ts">
	import { KeymapTable, Callout } from '#lib/index.ts';
</script>

Shortcuts apply while the viewport, or something inside it, has focus. Turn the viewer's off with `keyboard={false}` on `Viewer.Root`.

## Viewer

| Keys | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Ctrl/⌘ `+` / `=` · `-` · `0` | Zoom in · out · fit width |
| Ctrl/⌘ + wheel, trackpad pinch | Zoom (centred on narrow pages, under the cursor on wide ones) |
| ← → (when the page fits) · Home · End | Previous / next page · first · last |
| PageUp · PageDown · Space | Turn the page in single-page mode |
| Ctrl/⌘ `[` · `]` | Rotate |
| Alt + ← · → | Back / forward after a jump |

## Find

| Keys | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Ctrl/⌘ + F | Focus the find input (seeded with the selected text) |
| Enter · Shift + Enter | Next · previous match |
| Esc | Clear and return to the document |

## Annotations

Normal mode is **select**: read, select text, and double-click annotations to edit them. The table below is the live `defaultKeymap`:

<KeymapTable />

Remap any action through the `keymap` prop (merged over the defaults):

```svelte
<Annotations.Root keymap={{ 'tool.area': ['b'], undo: ['mod+z', 'alt+backspace'] }}>
```

Combos are written `mod+z` (Ctrl on Windows and Linux, ⌘ on macOS), `shift+mod+z`, `alt+1` or plain keys (`h`, `Delete`, `ArrowLeft`). `comboLabel(store.keymap, 'tool.area')` prints one for tooltips (`B`, `⌘Z`, `Ctrl+Z`).

<Callout>While typing in a note, plain digits type; use <kbd>Alt</kbd> + 1–9 to recolour. With `noteEmojis` set, the digits pick a note emoji instead of a color while the note tool is active or notes are selected. Enter keeps a new annotation (Shift + Enter adds a line), Esc discards it.</Callout>
